WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:06.770
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Agents of SHIELD we finally got to me Coulson’s

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.510
Cellist and there was a ton of awesome comic
book references.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.829
If you’re not watching, now is a really
good time to catch up because there’s only

00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:13.990
three more episodes left.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.509
In case you missed it, I also announced I’m
not doing a bonus Marvel Movie video this

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:25.150
week just because I’m working on some special
bonus videos for Arrow.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:26.730
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:31.000
So let’s talk some Agents of Playing Video
Games, who wouldn’t want to join that team.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.000
Here’s my top 5 moments.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.379
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:36.379 --> 00:00:43.230
Here we go, Number 5 - Coulson Tacks Down
Marcus Daniels

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.770
So many awesome things about about the infamous
list of meta-humans.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:50.640
It’s really Skye that calls out the superpowers
aspect of the list.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.160
Pretty much everyone in the Fridge has broken
out and they don’t really go too deep into

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.250
which super villains were in there, but Marcus
Daniels is the freak of the week.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.449
In the comics he becomes Blackout.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:13.600
I really appreciated that Coulson explained
the mechanism by which he gained powers.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.550
What is it about the Marvel Universe and cosmic
radiation?

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.170
All I could think about was the Fantastic
Four.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.720
It was a nice payoff to the Daniels arc that
Gamma Radiation based tech was the solution.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.960
Also providing a nice opportunity for a Hulk
shout out.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:36.550
The biggest question I had after Daniels explained
what happened to him in the Fridge was why?

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:41.650
Was it HYDRA scientists just conducting research
like Baron Von Strucker with Loki’s staff.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:46.510
If you didn’t catch it at the end of Captain
America, HYDRA is experimenting with super

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.540
powers, but Von Strucker had Loki’s staff.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.810
Which had the mind gem in it.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.340
We can talk more about that in another video.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:58.680
Number 4 - Patton Oswalt asks everyone what’s
in The Box?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.200
Every time someone asks that question I always
get a Seven flashback.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.930
I wonder if there’s an outtake with one
of the actors say “there’s a head, the

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.190
thing inside my mystery box is a human head”.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.050
The chair itself just felt like the ultimate
SHIELD geek chair, which was basically who

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:13.150
Agent Koenig was.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.379
He was like the ultimate Nick Fury fanboy.

00:02:16.379 --> 00:02:21.540
Which actually brings up a really good question
let me know who you think is a bigger Nick

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.180
Fury fanboy, Agent Koenig or Agent Coulson?

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.340
My favorite part of the interrogation scene
was that Doctor Who shout out from Simmons.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.459
Perfect answer.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:35.469
Although I feel like a more honest answer
would have been “The Doctor”.

00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:39.850
But if she had said that I feel like people
who don’t watch Doctor Who would have understood

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:40.879
what she meant.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:44.489
But everyone understands what the TARDIS is.

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:47.099
Be sure to let me know in the comments what’s
in your box.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.650
Number 3 - Ward makes his move on the hard
drive

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.430
I’m including him speechifying his backstory
in this.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:58.010
It makes it a little easier to put the pieces
together on how he ended up with Garrett.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.590
He said he rescued him from a bad situation.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.299
And I think he was being honest about his
brother and his parents.

00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:06.340
Garrett probably killed his parents and took
Ward into training.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.900
I think the show will probably explain this
in greater detail once the rest of the team

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.540
figures out he’s HYDRA.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.590
I was really bummed to see Patton Oswalt eat
it, but he will be avenged.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.969
If you didn’t catch it, the reason he had
to take Skye and the Bus to Peru is because

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:16.599
the hard drive can only be unlocked at specific
locations.

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:20.790
Number 2 - May Quits Team Coulson and Tracks
Down Maria Hill

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.219
Kind of two big things, but really I don’t
think anyone thinks May actually quit the

00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:27.349
team, she just needs some time.

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:31.000
But not only did we get to meet her mother,
who I’m guessing was a spy for the Chinese

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.420
Government or the Canadian Government or whoever.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.709
But May is going to track down Maria Hill.

00:03:36.709 --> 00:03:40.170
Marvel revealed she was coming back to the
show after Winter Soldier premiered.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.579
So it’s not a big surprise.

00:03:41.579 --> 00:03:44.859
We’ve know next week was going to be her
episode for a while.

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:49.469
I’m curious to see how she ends up helping
them, but as of right now.

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:54.409
She’s an employee at Stark Industries trying
to do something positive for humanity.

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:57.859
As opposed to invading everyone’s privacy
in the name of global security.

00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:02.370
Either way, expect several awesome Tony Stark
jokes next week.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.150
and my Number 1 moment - Amy Acker debuts
as The Cellist

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:10.280
The part was really short, but my favorite
Cellist moment was when she was explaining

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.700
how she met Coulson and their history together.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.220
I actually expected him to reveal himself,
but we can debate whether or not he should

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.000
have in the comments.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.880
If you never saw her on any of her other Joss
Whedon shows like Angel or Dollhouse.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.820
She also starred in his movie Much Ado About
Nothing.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.340
Which Clark Gregg was in.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:30.630
That’s an amazing movie all by itself, it’s
like whedonverse heaven.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.660
Seriously make sure you watch it.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.620
They were kind of vague on it, but that speech
from Couslon at the end about telling her

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.190
when the time was right just leaves the door
open for Amy Acker to come back in the future.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.060
If they do get a season 2.

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:53.130
She could always come back in a movie too.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.190
But let me know what you’re favorite moment
was?

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:01.250
Seeing the supervillain Blackout or meeting
the Cellist?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.230
For me it really was meeting that Cellist.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:08.320
She was such a huge teaser in the first Avengers
movie that I’m surprised they didn’t make

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.320
the cameo bigger.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:13.840
I guess we can pass that to tumblr to fill
in the gaps with fan fiction.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:19.510
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, I loved
the A story, that Cellist Marcus Daniels story.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:23.920
But I felt like the B story, Ward’s HYDRA
mission kind of pulled the episode down a

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:24.920
little.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.810
I just don’t feel like Chloe Bennett was
able to pull off the double agent scenes.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.050
I loved her and Ward before she discovered
his secret, but the way they edited the Patton

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.620
Oswalt reveal with the Cellist scenes didn’t
resonate with me.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:41.540
I just don’t think it works when Skye is
acting.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.730
Chloe Bennett acting ask Skye acting as secret
agent Skye trying to deceive Ward.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:49.560
I’m not a big fan of characters acting like
other characters.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.100
Unless it’s Tatiana Maslany on Orphan Black.

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.860
To be fair, the Cellist was such a huge pay
off.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.710
It’s been like one of the long con’s of
the Marvel Universe, this person that’s

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.130
so important to Coulson, but that we’ve
never met.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.410
And we’ve only been living with Patton Oswalt
for one week.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:08.820
I was really sad he had to die though.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:15.900
I’m hoping they eulogize him in some funny
way whenever they try to take down Ward and

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:16.900
Garrett.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.470
Let me know what you’re final thoughts are
on the episode and do you think Coulson should

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.870
have revealed himself to the Cellist?

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:29.300
Like I said, because I’m starting special
Arrow bonus videos there’s no Marvel Movie

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.300
video this week.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.930
I’m still going to do a couple Spider-Man
videos when that comes out in the United States

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:34.930
though.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.120
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.460
Right now click here for that Arrow Bonus
video and click here for last week’s Agents

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.460
Of SHIELD.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.200
Thanks so much for watching, see you guys
tomorrow.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:43.680
High Fives!

